@startuml
!theme plain
title ConfigWatcher State Machine

[*] --> Initializing : Create ConfigWatcher

state Initializing {
    [*] --> LoadingConfig
    LoadingConfig --> ValidatingSetup
    ValidatingSetup --> SetupInformer
    SetupInformer --> [*]
}

Initializing --> Watching : Start(ctx, ch)
Initializing --> Error : init failed

state Watching {
    [*] --> Idle
    Idle --> Listening : informer running
    Listening --> EventReceived : ConfigMap event
    EventReceived --> Idle : event queued

    note right of Listening
        Watching for ConfigMap
        changes with labels:
        - app=network-slicing
        - managed-by=mano
    end note
}

Watching --> Processing : ConfigMap event received

state Processing {
    [*] --> Filtering
    Filtering --> Validating : labels match
    Filtering --> [*] : labels don't match
    Validating --> Sending : validation pass
    Sending --> [*] : sent to channel

    note right of Filtering
        Filter by:
        - Label selectors
        - Namespace
        - Event type (Add/Update/Delete)
    end note
}

Processing --> Watching : event processed
Processing --> Error : processing failed

Watching --> Stopped : context cancelled
Error --> Stopped : shutdown
Stopped --> [*]

state Watching {
    Watching : entry / setup informer factory
    Watching : do / watch ConfigMaps continuously
    Watching : exit / cleanup informer
}

state Processing {
    Processing : entry / filter by labels
    Processing : do / validate and send to channel
    Processing : exit / log processing result
}

state Error {
    Error : entry / log error details
    Error : do / attempt recovery if possible
    Error : exit / cleanup resources
}

note top of Watching
    Main operational state
    Uses K8s informer pattern
end note

note bottom of Processing
    Non-blocking channel send
    with timeout protection
end note

@enduml